      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "[Ce(Me2pz)3(thf)]2 (0.27 g, 0.27 mmol) and K(OtBu) (0.061 g, 0.54 mmol) were stirred with heating at about 60 °C in toluene (5 mL) for two days in a greaseless Schlenk flask. The light-yellow powder was not entirely soluble in toluene, so THF (about 1 mL) was added. After several days the mixture was evaporated to dryness. Crystallization from hexane gave unsuitable colourless crystals, which were redissolved in fresh toluene (about 2 mL) and THF (about 2 mL) and heated at about 60 °C for several days. Addition of hexane and extended heating produced small orange crystals of the cerium(IV) polymer.",
